WEBVTT

00:01.280 --> 00:04.800
I was waiting for you. 
It's time to pay me back.

00:04.800 --> 00:05.690
Huh?

00:05.990 --> 00:11.890
Healer... Save my mother.

00:14.050 --> 00:15.150
Ooh!

00:15.470 --> 00:17.980
Who is this fox-eared girl, Usato-kun?!

00:17.980 --> 00:20.530
She's so cute! Can I pet her?

00:20.530 --> 00:23.150
You're the only one I can count on.

00:23.150 --> 00:25.620
I'm the only one? What do you mean?

00:25.620 --> 00:26.830
Completely ignored...

00:26.830 --> 00:30.000
You must really enjoy bullying me.

00:30.000 --> 00:33.490
Fine! I'll get excited all on my own!

00:33.490 --> 00:37.000
You're so annoying! 
Are you trying to be an attention hog?!

00:37.000 --> 00:38.220
Um...

00:39.260 --> 00:41.680
Please let me down for now.

00:41.680 --> 00:43.020
Oh, sorry.

00:44.530 --> 00:46.430
My name is Amako.

00:46.690 --> 00:49.290
As you can see, I'm a fox beastkin.

00:49.290 --> 00:51.570
I'd like to continue our 
conversation in private.

01:08.580 --> 01:13.260
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

02:24.200 --> 02:27.620
#13 The Journey Begins!

02:32.440 --> 02:35.010
Outta the way!

02:35.740 --> 02:38.850
What the hell? Pretty sloppy for a demon.

02:38.850 --> 02:42.980
Sh-Shut up! Don't lump me in with 
ogres and goblins like you!

02:42.980 --> 02:44.910
How rude!

02:44.910 --> 02:47.230
We're humans!

02:48.300 --> 02:51.410
They actually believe they're human?

02:51.410 --> 02:53.160
What strange creatures...

02:55.500 --> 02:57.100
I can't move.

02:57.100 --> 02:58.600
I don't care anymore.

02:58.600 --> 03:00.790
Just let me die here...

03:00.790 --> 03:02.530
No slacking off!

03:03.940 --> 03:07.120
Get running! You're not even halfway!

03:07.120 --> 03:09.050
Y-Yes, ma'am!

03:09.500 --> 03:13.380
The others are out training. 
We can talk safely here.

03:14.430 --> 03:17.370
She's so cute! I just want to rub those ears!

03:18.360 --> 03:21.930
Uh, are you sure you're 
all right with her here?

03:22.830 --> 03:24.110
It's fine.

03:24.110 --> 03:27.430
I'm sure a hero would keep my secret.

03:27.430 --> 03:29.220
Of course I will!

03:29.220 --> 03:31.110
So you know about her?

03:31.110 --> 03:32.530
I do.

03:32.530 --> 03:37.540
I also know your name is Usato, 
and that you use strange healing magic.

03:37.540 --> 03:40.320
I'll admit my healing magic is weird, but...

03:40.320 --> 03:41.520
Well, whatever.

03:41.900 --> 03:44.940
There are a lot of things I want to ask you.

03:44.940 --> 03:47.860
First, why did you show me that?

03:48.340 --> 03:51.900
The vision where Senpai and Kazuki 
were defeated by the Black Knight...

03:52.250 --> 03:54.170
What?! You saw a vision?!

03:54.170 --> 03:56.240
I had to show you.

03:56.540 --> 03:59.700
Otherwise, the heroes would die, 
and this kingdom would fall.

04:00.790 --> 04:04.340
Then it really was a prophetic vision...

04:05.210 --> 04:06.510
That's right.

04:06.510 --> 04:09.920
I have magic that lets me see the future.

04:09.920 --> 04:12.740
I had that vision a year ago,

04:12.740 --> 04:16.110
but I couldn't abandon the people 
who took care of me here.

04:16.380 --> 04:20.530
And most importantly, I couldn't lose 
you after I'd finally found you.

04:20.530 --> 04:24.310
Does that mean you've been
 looking for a healer?

04:24.310 --> 04:25.310
That's right.

04:25.310 --> 04:28.440
It's the reason I left the beastkin territory.

04:28.440 --> 04:32.540
Isn't the beastkin territory pretty far away?

04:32.540 --> 04:35.040
I had no choice.

04:35.040 --> 04:36.920
I have to save my mother.

04:37.440 --> 04:40.200
She hasn't opened her eyes in a long time.

04:40.200 --> 04:42.580
That's why I'm looking for a healer.

04:44.020 --> 04:48.400
I left beastkin territory because only 
humans can be born with healing magic.

04:48.400 --> 04:52.230
But there were no humans who would help me...

04:52.460 --> 04:55.720
And then you found Usato-kun in this kingdom.

04:55.720 --> 04:59.390
But why didn't you ask Orga-san 
or Ururu-san at the clinic?

04:59.750 --> 05:02.930
I'm sure they would've helped 
if you'd explained your situation.

05:03.320 --> 05:07.240
I can't take them with me 
because they can't fight.

05:07.730 --> 05:09.080
I see...

05:09.080 --> 05:10.450
Then what about Rose-san?

05:10.700 --> 05:13.330
I haven't spoken with that scary lady, either.

05:13.330 --> 05:15.820
I already had a vision of her rejecting me.

05:15.500 --> 05:20.170
<b>The hell?
I don't believe you.</b>

05:15.820 --> 05:16.580
Ah...

05:16.580 --> 05:20.170
Yeah, I guess that makes sense,
considering her position and all.

05:20.170 --> 05:22.320
And that leaves me, huh?

05:22.750 --> 05:25.710
I knew the moment I saw you
that you'd come with me.

05:25.710 --> 05:29.030
I could tell that's the kind of person you are.

05:29.030 --> 05:30.800
That's why I showed you the future.

05:31.300 --> 05:36.410
Usato, please come to the beastkin 
territory and save my mother.

05:37.970 --> 05:40.610
That's a rather difficult request.

05:40.610 --> 05:45.220
Usato-kun has become an important 
figure in this kingdom now.

05:48.800 --> 05:51.080
No, maybe I can do it.

05:51.080 --> 05:51.910
Huh?

05:51.910 --> 05:55.790
Senpai, didn't you hear about 
our journey to deliver missives?

05:55.790 --> 05:57.720
Yeah, I did.

05:57.720 --> 05:59.170
Wait, do you mean...

05:59.170 --> 06:00.130
Yes.

06:00.130 --> 06:04.520
Maybe I can stop by beastkin 
territory while we're traveling.

06:04.520 --> 06:05.600
I see.

06:05.880 --> 06:07.080
That might work.

06:07.080 --> 06:09.520
I'll have to ask King Lloyd.

06:09.520 --> 06:12.220
But first, I need to check with my captain.

06:13.160 --> 06:14.740
Can you wait a bit?

06:14.740 --> 06:15.550
Sure.

06:17.470 --> 06:22.870
Oh, and if you feel threatened by her, 
yell for help as loud as you can.

06:22.870 --> 06:26.580
Just who do you take me for, Usato-kun?!

06:26.580 --> 06:29.740
That beastkin girl is an Oracle of Time?

06:30.000 --> 06:31.150
You've gotta be kidding.

06:31.150 --> 06:32.370
Huh?

06:32.370 --> 06:34.570
I'll have to notify His Majesty immediately.

06:34.570 --> 06:36.730
Is it that serious?

06:36.730 --> 06:38.490
Very serious.

06:38.780 --> 06:42.280
Oracles of Time are responsible 
for predicting calamities

06:42.280 --> 06:44.460
and imparting that knowledge 
to the beastkin.

06:44.460 --> 06:47.170
If one of them has wound up in our kingdom,

06:47.170 --> 06:49.870
it could lead to war with 
the beastkin territory.

06:50.230 --> 06:51.560
I see...

06:51.820 --> 06:57.710
Well, even so, your wish 
to visit beastkin territory

06:57.710 --> 07:02.110
might just be possible <i>because</i> 
of our current circumstances.

07:02.110 --> 07:03.820
Wait for me.

07:03.820 --> 07:04.750
Okay.

07:07.570 --> 07:08.430
Thanks for waiting.

07:09.610 --> 07:10.290
Huh?

07:11.130 --> 07:14.450
I see. So it'll take a little while.

07:15.440 --> 07:17.900
<i>Did she predict what I was about to tell her?</i>

07:17.900 --> 07:20.450
You're talking to each other with your eyes!

07:20.450 --> 07:23.000
No fair! I feel like I've lost somehow!

07:23.000 --> 07:24.770
What are you talking about?

07:24.770 --> 07:26.140
Don't worry.

07:26.140 --> 07:28.800
I'm sure the king will think of something.

07:28.800 --> 07:31.210
Okay. I'll go home for today.

07:32.910 --> 07:34.060
Usato.

07:34.060 --> 07:35.130
Yes?

07:36.110 --> 07:37.300
Thank you.

07:39.840 --> 07:42.220
No, I should be the one thanking you.

07:42.650 --> 07:47.480
<i>I was able to save them thanks 
to you. Both Kazuki and Senpai.</i>

07:48.310 --> 07:49.160
What is it?

07:49.440 --> 07:51.170
Nothing at all.

07:52.410 --> 07:54.890
Good job, everyone!

08:00.860 --> 08:04.900
What?! Can't eat the food I make?!

08:04.900 --> 08:06.940
Shut up. Don't talk to me.

08:06.940 --> 08:08.550
You should eat.

08:09.310 --> 08:10.400
Usato...

08:10.400 --> 08:13.050
You'll pass out from hunger 
tomorrow if you don't.

08:13.780 --> 08:18.090
This hell is going to continue
 tomorrow and the day after?

08:18.090 --> 08:20.220
Just throw me back in prison.

08:22.990 --> 08:25.870
Here you go. I bought this
 at the market today.

08:27.740 --> 08:28.790
It's a diary.

08:29.990 --> 08:33.810
You should write down what you do 
each day and how you feel about it.

08:33.810 --> 08:36.230
It might make things a little easier.

08:55.800 --> 08:59.080
<i>I've decided to use the diary Usato gave me.</i>

08:59.100 --> 09:01.720
<b>Day 2</b>

08:59.100 --> 09:01.720
<b>Day 2</b>

08:59.640 --> 09:01.080
<i>My second day of training.</i>

09:01.080 --> 09:03.900
<i>I ran so much, I can't even move anymore.</i>

09:04.380 --> 09:05.410
<i>But...</i>

09:05.410 --> 09:07.310
Hey, what's wrong with you?

09:07.310 --> 09:08.480
Run!

09:11.570 --> 09:12.560
Keep it up!

09:12.560 --> 09:14.510
<i>Why the hell are they laughing?</i>

09:14.510 --> 09:16.590
<i>They're all crazy!</i>

09:16.700 --> 09:20.580
<b>Day 5</b>

09:16.800 --> 09:20.580
<b>Day 5</b>

09:17.340 --> 09:18.520
<i>Day five.</i>

09:18.520 --> 09:22.260
<i>Usato ran with us today, 
but something was weird.</i>

09:22.260 --> 09:25.330
<i>He didn't get winded the entire time.</i>

09:25.820 --> 09:30.040
<i>I've concluded that Usato 
is a human that isn't human.</i>

09:30.750 --> 09:32.670
<b>Day 10</b>

09:30.750 --> 09:32.670
<b>Day 10</b>

09:31.080 --> 09:32.260
<i>Day ten.</i>

09:32.670 --> 09:35.970
<i>Lately, I keep hearing noises 
from deep within the forest.</i>

09:36.880 --> 09:38.320
<i>What's going on in there?</i>

09:39.480 --> 09:42.160
<i>I decided to ditch training to take a peek.</i>

09:51.110 --> 09:53.030
<i>That definitely killed him!</i>

09:54.830 --> 09:55.950
<i>No way!</i>

09:58.380 --> 10:00.900
Hey, I told you to dodge!

10:00.900 --> 10:03.730
You're just getting better at taking hits!

10:04.280 --> 10:08.210
Your attack trajectory changes when I try! 
How the hell do I avoid that?!

10:08.210 --> 10:10.940
Just use your eyes and move!

10:10.940 --> 10:12.380
Like hell that'll work!

10:13.080 --> 10:15.020
<i>What's going on here?</i>

10:15.020 --> 10:17.320
Don't get all pissy with me now.

10:17.320 --> 10:18.750
Who's getting pissy here?!

10:18.750 --> 10:22.980
Save the big talk for after
 you avoid getting punched.

10:25.100 --> 10:26.340
Again!

10:26.340 --> 10:27.630
Bring it on!

10:34.230 --> 10:35.220
She disappeared!

10:43.830 --> 10:45.030
<i>He dodged it?!</i>

10:45.030 --> 10:46.460
All right! Finally!

10:46.460 --> 10:48.850
Don't let your guard down!

10:51.210 --> 10:52.870
A-Are you okay?

10:54.130 --> 10:57.290
Hell yeah! I dodged it!

10:56.240 --> 10:57.290
<i>Huh?!</i>

10:57.290 --> 10:59.040
I suppose you did well.

10:59.040 --> 11:01.100
You can return to regular training.

11:01.100 --> 11:02.800
Thank you very much!

11:03.500 --> 11:05.950
H-He's definitely not human.

11:05.950 --> 11:07.380
Hey, little brat.

11:07.380 --> 11:10.430
Keep training under Usato's orders.

11:11.020 --> 11:11.840
Huh?

11:12.930 --> 11:14.280
You saw, didn't you?

11:14.590 --> 11:17.180
The captain is a real monster.

11:17.460 --> 11:20.960
You look like you're becoming one yourself.

11:20.960 --> 11:22.980
Huh? What was that?

11:22.980 --> 11:24.030
Nothing.

11:26.480 --> 11:29.130
It's a little late, 
but can I ask you something?

11:30.670 --> 11:31.900
What is it?

11:33.570 --> 11:34.840
What's your name?

11:34.840 --> 11:37.170
That's late, all right.

11:37.170 --> 11:39.940
Sorry. I kept missing my chance.

11:40.900 --> 11:43.030
You want to know my name?

11:46.080 --> 11:47.890
I-It's Felm.

11:48.380 --> 11:51.140
Not many people call me that, though...

11:51.140 --> 11:52.830
I see. Got it.

11:52.830 --> 11:54.380
Oh, Blurin!

11:56.860 --> 11:59.010
You want to exercise, too?

11:59.010 --> 12:00.460
Okay, let's run together!

12:00.460 --> 12:01.650
Let's go!

12:02.490 --> 12:03.610
Hey...

12:04.110 --> 12:05.810
Is that all?

12:05.810 --> 12:07.250
Huh? Is what all?

12:10.780 --> 12:12.870
You asked for my name.

12:12.870 --> 12:15.560
I thought you'd at least say it or something...

12:15.560 --> 12:18.120
Hey, Blurin! Hold up!

12:19.420 --> 12:22.150
Damn it!

12:22.150 --> 12:24.920
Hey! You'll run out of steam 
if you keep up that pace!

12:24.920 --> 12:25.800
Shut up!

12:25.800 --> 12:27.850
I won't lose to you!

12:27.850 --> 12:29.760
What? She collapsed?

12:29.760 --> 12:33.430
Yeah. She went all-out with no 
consideration of pacing herself.

12:33.430 --> 12:37.110
But I healed her, and she's 
sleeping it off now.

12:33.430 --> 12:37.110
Shit! Damn Usato... Damn Usato...

12:33.440 --> 12:37.110
<b>Shit!
Damn Usato...
Damn Usato...</b>

12:37.110 --> 12:40.430
I swear... Take her meal to her later.

12:41.030 --> 12:42.070
Got it.

12:42.070 --> 12:45.120
What were you doing to that girl, Usato?

12:45.120 --> 12:47.210
Don't make it sound fishy.

12:47.210 --> 12:49.210
I was just running like normal.

12:49.210 --> 12:51.740
Your normal ain't normal.

12:51.740 --> 12:54.540
At the very least, not for humans!

12:55.670 --> 12:56.990
Shut up.

12:57.710 --> 12:59.870
I'm still more human than the captain!

13:16.010 --> 13:19.860
N-Now, everyone, it's not nice
to talk about people that way.

13:19.860 --> 13:21.590
I guess I said too much, too.

13:22.110 --> 13:24.780
Y-Yeah, we were wrong, too...

13:26.520 --> 13:27.810
Thrashing avoided.

13:27.810 --> 13:28.600
Hey, Usato.

13:28.600 --> 13:29.290
Yes?!

13:32.470 --> 13:34.960
So hungry...

13:36.400 --> 13:38.870
Go see His Majesty tomorrow morning.

13:39.550 --> 13:42.000
Take that fox beastkin with you.

13:42.000 --> 13:43.810
Huh? Does that mean...

13:43.810 --> 13:47.220
The details of your journey to deliver
 missives have been decided.

13:47.460 --> 13:51.170
I'm sure a decision has been made 
about your request, as well.

13:52.020 --> 13:53.060
I understand.

13:54.060 --> 13:57.980
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

13:54.370 --> 13:56.610
A journey to deliver missives?

14:23.280 --> 14:26.700
This is the first time I've 
ever entered the castle...

14:33.880 --> 14:36.060
You must be Amako.

14:36.060 --> 14:38.230
Y-Yes...

14:38.230 --> 14:41.570
Thank you for coming, Amako.

14:45.490 --> 14:50.990
I thank you from the bottom of my heart 
for saving our kingdom from certain doom.

14:51.820 --> 14:53.730
Huh? Um... Um...

14:53.730 --> 14:58.670
I would like to assist our nation's
 benefactor as best I can.

14:58.670 --> 15:00.140
So, Usato...

15:00.140 --> 15:01.700
Y-Yes!

15:01.700 --> 15:05.870
We have planned the route of your 
journey with your request in mind.

15:06.150 --> 15:10.420
After visiting various nations, we will have 
you deliver the final missive to Mialark.

15:11.050 --> 15:12.310
Mialark?

15:12.310 --> 15:16.800
It is a water nation built upon the 
great river that runs through the land.

15:16.800 --> 15:20.470
Far beyond its opposite shore
 lies the beastkin territory.

15:20.470 --> 15:21.650
Then...

15:21.650 --> 15:24.570
Yes. Take the opportunity to go with Amako.

15:25.850 --> 15:26.730
Right!

15:26.730 --> 15:28.440
Thank you very much!

15:28.440 --> 15:32.360
Welcie will discuss the rest with you.

15:32.360 --> 15:35.220
Yes, please leave the details to me.

15:35.840 --> 15:39.990
Now, you will be visiting
 four different territories.

15:40.460 --> 15:42.180
The city of magic, Luqvist.

15:40.460 --> 15:44.400
<b>Demon Territory</b>

15:40.460 --> 15:44.650
<b>Luqvist</b>

15:40.460 --> 15:45.310
<b>Llinger Kingdom</b>

15:40.460 --> 15:48.380
<b>*In Usato's translated perspective</b>

15:40.460 --> 15:48.380
<b>Samariarl</b>

15:40.460 --> 15:48.380
<b>Mialark</b>

15:40.460 --> 15:48.380
<b>Beastkin Territory</b>

15:42.180 --> 15:43.880
The nation of prayer, Samariarl.

15:43.880 --> 15:45.560
The nation of water, Mialark.

15:45.560 --> 15:48.380
And, finally, the beastkin territory.

15:48.380 --> 15:52.800
Dame Suzune, Sir Kazuki, and I 
will accompany you to Luqvist.

15:53.040 --> 15:58.230
After that, you will part ways along with 
Miss Amako and your attending knights.

15:58.230 --> 16:01.890
Attending knights? 
How many are coming with us?

16:02.220 --> 16:06.620
Taking too many knights will make 
foreign nations suspicious...

16:06.620 --> 16:08.630
So perhaps two or so.

16:08.630 --> 16:11.780
Would you like me to suggest 
a few knights for you?

16:13.060 --> 16:14.980
Huh? Me?

16:14.980 --> 16:17.930
Yes. Please come with us.

16:19.640 --> 16:20.910
Would you rather not?

16:21.730 --> 16:25.230
Sir Usato, I'm a clumsy man.

16:25.230 --> 16:27.850
I can't protect more 
than one thing at a time.

16:28.420 --> 16:29.580
Right.

16:29.580 --> 16:31.860
That's why I chose to protect this place.

16:32.260 --> 16:35.490
As long as it's guarded, no one can invade.

16:35.490 --> 16:38.680
The people inside are safe.

16:38.680 --> 16:40.520
So I guess...

16:40.520 --> 16:44.410
But I'll have my comrades protect 
the castle for a little while.

16:46.360 --> 16:53.370
I, sworn knight Aruku, will protect 
Sir Usato and Miss Amako with my life!

16:53.370 --> 16:56.040
Thank you! We're counting on you!

16:56.040 --> 16:58.410
I'm glad things were settled so easily!

16:58.410 --> 17:01.040
Who would you like as your second knight?

17:01.040 --> 17:02.590
Let me think...

17:02.590 --> 17:04.460
What about him?

17:04.460 --> 17:05.300
Huh?

17:21.300 --> 17:24.220
And here I thought you'd quieted down a bit.

17:24.220 --> 17:27.620
I didn't think you'd take this chance to run.

17:27.970 --> 17:30.650
Looks like you've gotten a little too spoiled.

17:32.070 --> 17:36.580
You overheard us talking about the journey 
to deliver missives yesterday, didn't you?

17:36.580 --> 17:41.210
For a second, I thought you'd fled 
to notify the Demon Lord's army...

17:41.740 --> 17:46.540
But I'm guessing not, considering how 
close you still are to the dormitory.

17:48.090 --> 17:49.960
Aren't you worried?

17:49.960 --> 17:52.180
Worried? About what?

17:53.230 --> 17:57.060
Usato is traveling really far away, right?

17:58.470 --> 18:01.400
Oh, that. There's nothing to worry about.

18:01.670 --> 18:06.460
He's a healer very similar to me.

18:06.460 --> 18:08.310
He won't get hurt easily.

18:09.730 --> 18:11.550
Hmm? What?

18:11.550 --> 18:13.900
Could it be that <i>you're</i> worried about him?

18:14.170 --> 18:17.790
Were you planning on hiding here 
and following him on his journey?

18:17.790 --> 18:20.070
N-No! Of course not!

18:20.070 --> 18:24.020
I'm just sick of living like this! That's all!

18:24.020 --> 18:26.350
Oh? Sick of it, are you?

18:26.350 --> 18:29.110
Guess it's about time to take you over <i>there</i>.

18:29.110 --> 18:30.880
What? Over where?

18:30.880 --> 18:34.830
Oh, we won't go right away. 
Let's head back to the dormitory first.

18:34.830 --> 18:36.050
Get running!

18:37.260 --> 18:39.760
I can't believe you tried to escape.

18:39.760 --> 18:40.840
That's impressive.

18:43.570 --> 18:45.510
You're leaving on a journey.

18:45.510 --> 18:48.560
Yeah. I'm leaving tomorrow.

18:50.390 --> 18:51.390
What's wrong?

18:52.350 --> 18:55.770
Oh, could it be that you're going
to miss me when I'm gone?

18:58.180 --> 19:01.400
It's not fair that you're escaping 
from this hell by yourself!

19:01.400 --> 19:02.610
That's all!

19:02.610 --> 19:04.530
Oh, so that's what it is.

19:05.650 --> 19:07.840
You, you, you...

19:06.790 --> 19:10.830
Hey, hey! Don't kick me so much, Felm.

19:17.040 --> 19:19.110
What's up with her?

19:19.710 --> 19:22.370
Leaving tomorrow is pretty sudden.

19:22.850 --> 19:24.530
What are you talking about?

19:24.530 --> 19:27.810
You're the one who sent me to the 
Darkness of Llinger without any notice.

19:29.200 --> 19:30.730
True.

19:30.730 --> 19:33.700
But, well, this trip is different.

19:33.700 --> 19:35.890
Let me tell you one thing before you go.

19:36.360 --> 19:37.670
What is it?

19:37.670 --> 19:43.560
Many people consider healing magic 
weaker than other types of magic.

19:44.450 --> 19:49.000
But if you ever meet anyone 
who tells you that...

19:50.500 --> 19:52.930
Beat 'em to a pulp and don't hold back.

19:53.280 --> 19:55.540
Isn't that a little too violent?!

19:55.540 --> 19:59.560
If you give someone who judges 
others at face value a beating,

19:59.560 --> 20:03.210
they tend to become more world-wise.

20:03.210 --> 20:04.090
Huh?

20:07.520 --> 20:13.440
I'm sure this journey to deliver missives 
will affect you one way or another.

20:21.690 --> 20:24.080
I expect great things from you, Usato.

20:29.450 --> 20:32.050
<i>She expects great things, huh?</i>

20:34.760 --> 20:37.860
<i>Damn it... That makes me happy.</i>

20:39.280 --> 20:41.470
<i>I know I'm a pretty simple guy.</i>

20:41.470 --> 20:45.050
<i>But in the end, I really trust her.</i>

20:47.300 --> 20:50.470
<i>I admire her as my teacher.</i>

20:52.190 --> 20:55.470
<i>I'll keep living in this world.</i>

20:56.560 --> 21:00.150
<i>Together with her and the 
people of this kingdom.</i>

21:06.220 --> 21:07.870
Do your best, Usato.

21:07.870 --> 21:09.980
Though it might be a tough journey...

21:09.980 --> 21:11.450
Make sure you eat well,

21:11.450 --> 21:14.620
sleep well, and don't worry too 
much about annoying stuff!

21:14.620 --> 21:15.640
Right...

21:32.680 --> 21:33.950
Usato.

21:36.270 --> 21:39.030
I'll be by your side, Amako.

21:40.510 --> 21:41.320
Yeah.

21:42.030 --> 21:43.930
Please take care.

21:43.930 --> 21:45.460
Yeah, we'll be back.

21:45.460 --> 21:49.280
We'll be sure to return with good news, Celia.

21:49.280 --> 21:51.670
I'm sure. I believe in you all.

21:53.480 --> 21:54.540
Open the gates!

21:56.240 --> 21:58.040
Now, let us depart!

21:59.760 --> 22:03.250
<i>New nations and new people...</i>

22:03.850 --> 22:07.040
<i>I wonder what will happen 
from here on out.</i>

22:36.090 --> 22:41.280
Wh-Where in the world are you taking me?

23:02.680 --> 23:03.940
Come on!

23:03.940 --> 23:05.360
Don't dawdle!

23:05.360 --> 23:07.300
Y-Yes, ma'am!

23:10.180 --> 23:11.530
Usato-kun!

23:18.420 --> 23:21.590
<i>A new journey to new places.</i>

23:21.590 --> 23:24.040
<i>A great adventure full of 
danger and the unknown.</i>

23:24.680 --> 23:28.120
<i>For better or worse, 
I've integrated myself into this world.</i>

23:28.120 --> 23:33.470
<i>And as the carriage sways, my thoughts 
turn to my upcoming journey.</i>

23:33.800 --> 23:40.010
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>
